WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.480
Private retrieval-augmented generation is an architecture pattern for grounding AI

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.360
responses in controlled source material.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.680
Instead of relying only on what a model already learned during training,

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.440
the system retrieves documents, policies, procedures, tickets, product notes,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.180
code guidance,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.135
or other approved knowledge and provides that material as context for the answer.

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:21.661
The private part adds requirements that a simple demonstration may ignore.

00:00:21.661 --> 00:00:24.890
A demo can upload a few files and return a plausible response.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.814
A production private RAG system has to preserve source ownership, classification,

00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:33.035
ingestion date, access rules, tenant boundaries, freshness, citations, logging,

00:00:33.035 --> 00:00:35.490
deletion expectations, and operational support.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:39.310
RAG does not make information automatically correct or automatically authorized.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.010
Retrieved material is evidence for the model to consider,

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.870
not an unlimited source of authority.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.810
The architecture still needs rules about which source wins when guidance conflicts,

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.240
how stale material is handled,

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.365
and when the system should decline to answer or ask for review.

00:00:52.365 --> 00:00:56.190
Good private RAG design makes source visibility part of the user experience and the

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.105
operating model.

00:00:57.105 --> 00:01:00.040
Users and reviewers should be able to understand where an answer came from,

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.010
why those sources were selected, and whether the content is current enough for the task.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.570
The value of private RAG is not just better answers.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.080
It is accountable answers. The system is strongest when retrieval, permissions,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:10.640
provenance,

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.635
and lifecycle controls are designed together so users can trust the answer and the

00:01:14.635 --> 00:01:15.680
boundary behind it.
